cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Agentic-AI Containment RCSA: A Reusable Instrument with Two Worked Examples"
message: "If you use this material, please cite it as below."
type: dataset
authors:
  - name: "socragpt"
abstract: >-
  An independent, open Risk & Control Self-Assessment (RCSA) instrument for the
  frontier-AI model-evaluation, training-environment-integrity and agent-containment
  process. Shipped as a blank, fillable instrument (risk register, control library,
  action plan, KRI/KCI register, risk-appetite model and auto-calculating profile
  summary) with a methodology and an AI-agent playbook, and demonstrated by two
  worked examples: the 2026 OpenAI-Hugging Face agent-containment incident, and
  Anthropic's July-September 2026 post-incident response (evaluation and training
  safety). Each example ships a populated workbook, a narrative report and an
  interactive matrix. Compiled solely from public sources; not affiliated with or
  endorsed by OpenAI, Hugging Face or Anthropic.
version: "1.1"
